help could be on the way for america's  wild horse herds nevada congresswoman  dina titus plans to ban the use of  helicopters during often brutal  round-ups of the mustangs eight news now  chief i-team reporter george knapp is  here with his exclusive story the niece  and brian we've all seen these videos of  herds of wild mustangs running in terror  as blm contractors swoop out of the sky  stampeding the frightened animals across  rough terrain horrific injuries and  deaths of horses are now the norm they  happen pretty much every time there's a  roundup it's admittedly hard to watch  images like this one from a recent  operation at nevada's pancake complex  our i-team colleague vanessa murphy  reported about this young horse running  for its life despite an obviously broken  leg that animal and others had to be put  down and your money pays for all of this  since 2011 blm has forked over 36  million dollars to a handful of private  contractors to carry out roundups in  nevada and other western states it cost  more than 500 dollars per horse to  capture them congresswoman dina titus  saw the same video you just saw and  decided enough was enough  tomorrow morning she'll introduce  legislation to ban the use of  helicopters in wild horse roundups  but the roundups with helicopters are  the worst you saw the pictures from the  most recent one at the pancake area near  ely where they chased that little cult  tilly just ran down and then they had to  shoot them what purpose does that serve  so we need to find another method and  the first thing we can do is get rid of  outlaw ban those helicopters  a century ago there were more than two  million wild horses in america today  there are about seventy thousand more  than half of them here in nevada but  that's still too many according to blm  which plans to gather more of them this  year than ever before representative  titus says she'll introduce her bill  tomorrow morning and she expects to  garner bipartisan support you know  barring the use of helicopters would  mean blm would have to use methods that  don't create the same kind of stark  terror among the mustangs titus says her  slogan for this proposal is to quote  save a horse hire a cowboy we'll have  more on that proposal tomorrow evening
 

